<% content_for :title, "Readme – Sage Timer" %>

<div class="tools-page">
  <h1>Readme</h1>

  <section class="tools-section">
    <h2>About Sage Timer</h2>
    <div class="tools-content">
      <p>Sage Timer is a lane scheduling and timing management application for swim meets. It helps meet organizers, coaches, officials, and lane timers coordinate lane assignments and bookings.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="tools-section">
    <h2>Features</h2>
    <ul class="tools-list">
      <li>Lane schedule dashboard with drag-and-drop booking management</li>
      <li>Lanes 1–10 support A/B sub-lane timers; Lanes 0 and 11 are single-timer lanes</li>
      <li>Club and workout group management with bookable status tracking</li>
      <li>Meet and session configuration</li>
      <li>Booking list with sorting, searching, and club filtering</li>
      <li>Role-based access control (Admin, Lane Timer, Official, Meet Management, Coach)</li>
      <li>Tools page with meet information, FAQs, links, and downloadable files</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="tools-section">
    <h2>User Roles</h2>
    <ul class="tools-list">
      <li><strong>Admin / COMSA</strong> — Full access to all features including user, meet, and session management</li>
      <li><strong>Lane Timer</strong> — Access to schedule, bookings, clubs, and tools</li>
      <li><strong>Official</strong> — Access to schedule, bookings, clubs, and tools</li>
      <li><strong>Meet Management</strong> — Access to schedule, bookings, clubs, and tools</li>
      <li><strong>Coach</strong> — Access to schedule, bookings, clubs, and tools</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="tools-section">
    <h2>Getting Started</h2>
    <div class="tools-content">
      <p>Log in with your assigned username and password, or <%= link_to "create a new account", signup_path, style: "color: var(--primary); text-decoration: underline;" %> to get started.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</div>
